Yes, creating a unified API is the exact right approach here. Instead of making the React frontend fire multiple separate requests to piece this together, we can write a single, highly optimized SQL JOIN in the backend. This reduces network latency and keeps your React components clean.
Here is how to build this aggregated API and display the data beautifully in the modal.
### Step 1: Create the Aggregated API (Java Backend)
We will join all three tables (VOUCHER_POSTING, REQUEST_VOUCHER, and VOUCHER_CATEGORY) using the BATCH_ID.
**1. Add this method to your VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java:**
```java
    @Override
    public Map<String, Object> getBatchSummaryDetails(String batchId) {
        String sql = """
            SELECT 
                vp.VID_FK AS VID,
                vp.CREATED_BY AS BATCH_CREATED_BY,
                vp.CREATED_AT AS BATCH_CREATED_AT,
                vp.CREATORS_ROLE,
                vp.SCHEDULED_TIME,
                vp.EXECUTED_AT,
                vc.CATEGORY_NAME,
                rv.DESCRIPTION,
                rv.REMARKS AS VID_REMARKS
            FROM VOUCHER_POSTING vp
            LEFT JOIN REQUEST_VOUCHER rv ON vp.VID_FK = rv.VID
            LEFT JOIN VOUCHER_CATEGORY vc ON rv.CATEGORY_ID = vc.ID
            WHERE vp.BATCH_ID = ?
        """;
        
        try {
            return jdbcTemplate.queryForMap(sql, batchId);
        } catch (EmptyResultDataAccessException e) {
            return new HashMap<>(); // Return empty if batch not found
        }
    }

```
*(Make sure to add Map<String, Object> getBatchSummaryDetails(String batchId); to your interface as well).*
**2. Expose the API in your Controller:**
```java
    @GetMapping("/batch-summary/{batchId}")
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, Object>> getBatchSummaryDetails(@PathVariable String batchId) {
        return ResponseEntity.ok(voucherRequestService.getBatchSummaryDetails(batchId));
    }

```
### Step 2: Update React State & API Call
Now we update JournalAuthorization.jsx to call this new endpoint instead of the old vid-details one.
**1. Find your handleOpenViewModal function and update the Promise.all block:**
```javascript
  const handleOpenViewModal = async (row) => {
    setViewingBatch(row);
    setViewingBatchId(row.batchId);
    setViewingBatchCreatorId(String(row.creatorId));
    setViewingBatchState(row.workflowState || "PENDING_L1");

    setIsViewModalOpen(true);
    setIsFetchingSteps(true);
    setIsFetchingVid(true); // Reusing this state for the summary data

    try {
      const workflowCode = row.approvalWorkflow || "Workflow_3";
      
      // CHANGE: Fetching the unified batch-summary API instead of just VID
      const [stepsData, summaryData] = await Promise.all([
        callApi(`/JS/voucher/workflow/steps/${workflowCode}`, null, "GET"),
        callApi(`/JS/voucher/batch-summary/${row.batchId}`, null, "GET") 
      ]);
      
      let fetchedSteps = Array.isArray(stepsData) ? [...stepsData] : [];

      fetchedSteps = fetchedSteps.map(step => {
         if (step.state === 'POSTED' || step.state === 'APPROVED') {
             return { ...step, designation: 'Executed', role: 'System' };
         }
         return step;
      });

      if (!fetchedSteps.find(s => s.state === 'POSTED' || s.designation === 'Executed')) {
          fetchedSteps.push({ state: 'POSTED', designation: 'Executed', role: 'System' });
      }
      
      setDynamicSteps(fetchedSteps);
      
      // Save the combined data to state
      setVidDetails(summaryData); 
    } catch (err) {
      showSnackBar("Failed to load batch summary.", "error");
    } finally {
      setIsFetchingSteps(false);
      setIsFetchingVid(false);
    }
  };

```
